n        [Assumption \u2014 80% of FY26 capex] \u2212 \u0394WC ~0.60 [Estimate based on\n        AR+Inv delta of 0.60 between FY25 and FY26 [Arithmetic]]\n        \u2248 $5.66B [Estimate].\n        Owner-earnings yield = 5.66 / 119.505 = 4.7% [Arithmetic].\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3 \u2014 VALUATION (ENGINE 1: DCF + MULTIPLES)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n3.1   Discount-rate derivation:\n      - Risk-free (10Y UST): 4.65% [Actual - FRED, 2026-08-21].\n      - Equity risk premium: 4.50% [Assumption].\n      - Beta: 0.75 [Assumption; vendor reports 0.566 [Aggregator] but window/\n        benchmark unknown; 0.75 better reflects medical-device cyclicality and\n        FDA/tariff exposure].\n      - Cost of equity = 4.65 + 0.75(4.50) = 8.03% [Arithmetic].\n      - Pre-tax cost of debt: 4.50% [Estimate \u2014 A-rated med-tech spread over\n        4.65% 10Y; pack interest expense implies ~3% coupon but refinancing\n        risk makes 4.5% the right marginal cost].\n      - Tax rate: 16% [Estimate \u2014 MDT non-GAAP nominal tax rate; GAAP ETR not\n        fully derivable from pack].\n      - After-tax cost of debt = 4.50%(1\u22120.16) = 3.78% [Arithmetic].\n      - Weights: E = 119.505 / (119.505+27.961) = 81.0%;\n        D = 27.961 / 147.466 = 19.0% [Arithmetic].\n      - WACC = 0.810(8.03%) + 0.190(3.78%) = 6.50 + 0.72 = 7.22% \u2248 7.2%\n        [Arithmetic].\n      - Base WACC used: 7.5% [Assumption \u2014 add ~30bps for FX volatility,\n        tariff/regulatory event risk not captured in beta; range 7.0\u20138.0%].\n3.2   Forecast path \u2014 explicit per year, FY27E\u2013FY36E ($B) [Assumptions in\n      brackets; each line tied to a source]:\n      Revenue growth:\n        FY27: +7.0% \u2192 $38.91B [Actual guidance 6.75\u20137.25% organic, incl. 53rd\n        week; no material FX assumption. Source: Medtronic June 3, 2026 release].\n        FY28: +5.5% \u2192 $41.05B [Assumption \u2014 above 5-yr CAGR 3.8% because PFA/\n        Hugo ramp; fading].\n        FY29: +5.0% \u2192 $43.10B [Assumption].\n        FY30: +4.5% \u2192 $45.04B [Assumption \u2014 industry CAGR ~5.4% per\n        MarketsandMarkets [Estimate]; large-cap discount).\n        FY31: +4.5% \u2192 $47.06B [Assumption].\n        FY32: +4.0% \u2192 $48.95B [Assumption].\n        FY33: +4.0% \u2192 $50.91B [Assumption].\n        FY34: +3.5% \u2192 $52.69B [Assumption].\n        FY35: +3.5% \u2192 $54.54B [Assumption].\n        FY36: +3.0% \u2192 $56.17B [Assumption \u2014 near long-run nominal GDP].\n        Long-term terminal growth: 3.0% [Assumption \u2014 = long-run nominal GDP].\n      GAAP operating margin (OI):\n        FY26 actual: 17.8% [Arithmetic on filed OI $6.467B / rev $36.364B].\n        FY27\u2013FY36: 17.9%, 18.2%, 18.5%, 18.7%, 18.9%, 19.1%, 19.2%, 19.3%,\n        19.4%, 19.5% [Assumption \u2014 gradual recovery toward FY18 peak 22.2%\n        [Arithmetic], capped at 19.5% to remain conservative; FY27 guided EPS\n        +7% on revenue +7% implies margin roughly flat [Estimate]].\n      Tax rate: 16% [Estimate].\n      D&A as % of revenue: 8.0% FY27\u201328; 7.5% FY29\u201330; 7.0% FY31\u201332; 6.5%\n        FY33\u201336 [Assumption \u2014 FY26 = 8.1% [Arithmetic]; intangibles amortization\n        fades as Covidien intangibles age].\n      Capex as % of revenue: 5.0% every year [Assumption \u2014 FY26 = 5.2%\n        [Arithmetic]; 12-yr range 3.5\u20135.8% [Arithmetic]].\n      \u0394NWC: 0.30% of revenue each year [Assumption \u2014 historical \u0394 non-cash WC\n        (AR+Inv) FY26 = +$0.60B \u2248 1.7% of revenue [Arithmetic], but lumpy;\n        normalized long-term drag 0.3%].\n      SBC expense: 1.25% of revenue each year [Assumption \u2014 FY26 = 0.457/36.364\n        = 1.26% [Arithmetic]].\n\n      FCFF definition: EBIT\u00d7(1\u22120.16) + D&A \u2212 Capex \u2212 \u0394NWC \u2212 SBC.\n      Forecast table ($B):\n      FY    Rev    EBIT%  EBIT   NOPAT  D&A   Capex  \u0394NWC  SBC   FCFF\n      FY27  38.91  17.9%  6.965  5.851  3.113 1.946 0.117 0.486 6.415\n      FY28  41.05  18.2%  7.471  6.276  3.284 2.052 0.123 0.513 6.872\n      FY29  43.10  18.5%  7.974  6.698  3.233 2.155 0.129 0.539 7.108\n      FY30  45.04  18.7%  8.422  7.074  3.378 2.252 0.135 0.563 7.502\n      FY31  47.06  18.9%  8.894  7.471  3.294 2.353 0.141 0.588 7.683\n      FY32  48.95  19.1%  9.349  7.853  3.426 2.447 0.147 0.612 8.073\n      FY33  50.91  19.2%  9.775  8.211  3.564 2.545 0.153 0.636 8.441\n      FY34  52.69  19.3% 10.169  8.542  3.425 2.635 0.158 0.659 8.515\n      FY35  54.54  19.4% 10.581  8.888  3.545 2.727 0.164 0.682 8.860\n      FY36  56.17  19.5% 10.953  9.200  3.651 2.809 0.169 0.702 9.171\n      [All arithmetic on the above; growth/margin/capex/etc. sourced in the\n      bullet points above.]\n3.3   Terminal value:\n      Base WACC 7.5%, g 3.0%:\n        TV = 9.171 \u00d7 1.03 / (0.075 \u2212 0.03) = 9.446 / 0.045 = $209.9B\n        [Arithmetic].\n      Present value factors at 7.5%:\n        FY27 0.930, FY28 0.865, FY29 0.805, FY30 0.749, FY31 0.696,\n        FY32 0.648, FY33 0.603, FY34 0.561, FY35 0.522, FY36 0.485\n        [Arithmetic].\n   