0\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n8.1   Thesis integrity criteria (breach = re-analyze):\n      - Organic revenue growth: FY27 guide 6.75\u20137.25% [Actual]; WATCH if two\n        consecutive quarters <4.5%; BREACH if <3%.\n      - Cardiac Ablation Solutions revenue growth: Q4 FY26 +78% [Actual];\n        WATCH if <30%; BREACH if <15%.\n      - GAAP OI margin: FY26 17.8% [Arithmetic]; WATCH if <17.0%; BREACH if\n        <16.0% for two quarters.\n      - Adjusted EPS: guide $5.90\u20136.00 [Actual]; WATCH if $5.70\u20135.90; BREACH\n        if <$5.70.\n      - FCF conversion from adj. net income: 76% FY26 [Actual \u2014 release];\n        WATCH if <65%; BREACH if <55%.\n      - Net debt/adj. EBITDA: ~2.1x [Estimate]; BREACH if >2.75x.\n      - MiniMed retained stake: track mark-to-market value (90.03% retained\n        [Actual \u2014 investing.com/company release]); BREACH if writedown\n        exceeds $1.0B.\n      - Tariff impact: FY26 = 50bps [Actual]; BREACH if >150bps.\n8.2   Pre-mortem \u2014 \"If MDT fails in 5 years, why?\"\n      Failure scenario 1: PFA becomes a commodity pricing war (BSX Farapulse\n      + J&J/others); MDT gains 8pts share only to give back 6pts by 2029.\n      Early warning: PFA growth decelerates from 78% to <25% while ASPs fall\n      >10% y/y.\n      Failure scenario 2: Hugo cannot dislodge Intuitive; cumulative losses\n      >$2B with <20% hospital attach rate. Early warning: robot placements\n      <40/quarter and procedure growth <30%/quarter.\n      Failure scenario 3: MiniMed separation destroys $6\u20138B of shareholder\n      value via stranded intercompany costs and BM/US litigation.\n      Early warning: MiniMed trades below IPO price for 6+ months, triggering\n      goodwill impairment at MDT.\n8.3   Decision journal entry \u2014 see Section 11.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 9 \u2014 RED TEAM & ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n9.1   Short thesis (same data):\n      1. FY26 non-GAAP operating margin was DOWN 130bps (150bps constant\n         currency) [Actual \u2014 release]; FY27 EPS guide $5.90\u20136.00 MISSED\n         consensus $6.06 [Estimate \u2014 StocksToTrade] \u2014 margin recovery is a\n         hope, not a trend.\n      2. The \"10-year-best growth\" is partly COVID comps + 53rd week and FX:\n         FY26 reported +8.4% vs organic +5.8% [Actual]; FY27 organic includes\n         a 53rd-week extra \u2014 true underlying run-rate \u22485%.\n      3. $27.961B debt [Aggregator] at rising rates: interest expense will\n         increase by ~$150\u2013200M/yr on refinancing [Assumption], offsetting\n         margin gains.\n      4. MiniMed: $560M IPO, MDT retains 90% [Actual \u2014 Investing.com]; the\n         remaining-distribution overhang plus a low valuation for a growing\n         asset signals value destruction.\n      5. Tariffs: 50bps OM impact FY26 [Actual]; med-device tariffs and a\n         strong dollar [Unconfirmed] pressure both margins and revenue.\n      6. Activism (Elliott [Estimate \u2014 research brief]) reduces management\n         bandwidth and can force leverage-increasing M&A or poor exits.\n      7. GAAP ROIC \u2248 7% [Estimate] is BELOW WACC \u2014 the business earns less\n         than its cost of capital on an adjusted basis; \"quality-compounder\"\n         classification is generous.\n9.2   Logic combat:\n      Long thesis score: 7/10. Short thesis score: 6/10.\n      Gap = 1 (< 2) \u2192 Conviction downgrade applied (Section 5).\n      Core long advantage: filing-based cash generation ($5.426B FCF FY26\n      [Arithmetic]) is real; PFA/Hugo optionality is free at the current\n      no-growth price.\n      Core short advantage: margin trend is genuinely negative; revenue growth\n      contains artificial boosts (53rd week, easy comps, FX).\n9.3   Adversarial data: no current Hindenburg-type report exists [Unconfirmed];\n      risk-factor screen at TipRanks shows 34 regulatory risks [Estimate \u2014\n      research brief]. No accounting red flags in pack: Piotroski 7/7,\n      accruals \u22120.0274 [Arithmetic \u2014 filed-derived].\n9.4   Killed arguments:\n      - \"Hugo is a robotics game-changer\": killed at 50% weight because\n        Intuitive's installed base and procedural ecosystem dwarf MDT;\n        valid again only if Hugo placements exceed 100/quarter.\n      - \"PFA makes MDT a growth stock\": killed because cardiac ablation is\n        <10% of total revenue [Estimate]; valid again only if CV organic\n        sustains >9% for 8+ quarters.\n      - \"Spinoffs always create value\": killed because MiniMed's IPO priced\n        soft; valid again only if MMED trades >$25 [Unconfirmed price] and\n        MDT distributes the stake tax-free.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 10 \u2014 AUDIT RESULTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n10.1  37-point audit summary:\n      A. Methodology (6/6): Engine selection documented; no DCF-only\n         conclusion; no multiple-only conclusion; no TAM-only conclusion;\n         macro incorporated; base rates incorporated.\n      B. Valuation (8/8): Discount rate derived from market/filed data;\n         explicit forecast table; terminal value bounded to nominal GDP;\n         reverse DCF performed; tornado sensitivity on top-3 variables;\n         EBIT vs FCF definition reconciled to OCF/capex; SBC deducted;\n         no double-count of cash/debt (vendor debt reconciled to LT-noncurrent\n         + current portion: $26.173B + $1.788B = $27.961B \u2713 [Arithmetic]).\n      C. Bias (6/6): 50%/80% CIs shown; Bayesian update; no anchoring to\n         analyst target; bear case uses same data; single-point estimates\n         avoided; [Unconfirmed] items carried through scenarios.\n      D. Consistency (4/4): T0 price used consistently; time-point discipline;\n         no mixing of GAAP and non-GAAP in the FCFF path; per-share\n         calculations use T0 share count.\n      E. Narrative (4/4): PFA/Hugo claims quantified; \"long-term potential\"\n         phrase not used; every forecast driver sourced or labelled\n         [Assumption]; segment gaps declared.\n      F. Red team (6/6): bulleted short thesis; logic-combat scored; killed\n         arguments documented; adversarial data checked; pre-mortem carried;\n         poison-pill conditions defined.\n      G. Data integrity (3/4): one conditional item \u2014 R&D figure sourced from\n         third party [Estimate], not a filing; segment data absent [Known gap];\n         analyst Q&A absent [Known gap]; TTM anchor stranded [Known gap].\n      PASS: 36/37 conditional pass. MODEL CONFIDENCE: Medium-High.\n10.2  Data-gap declaration:\n      - Segment revenue/margin: ZERO dimensional rows in pack [Declared].\n      - R&D expense: not in pack; sourced from Macrotrends [Estimate].\n      - FY26 interest expense: not in pack [Unconfirmed].\n      - DXY and credit spreads: not retrieved [Unconfirmed].\n      - Analyst Q&A/assumptions underlying FY27 guidance: not held.\n      These gaps bound the 80% CI to \u00b1$23/share.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 11 \u2014 DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n11.1  T0: 2026-08-24. Price $93.35 [Aggregator].\n      Zone: LOW end of fair value ($102 \u00b1 10).\n      Base IV: ~$102 [Estimate]; MoS \u2248 8% (Limited).\n      Key assumptions at entry:\n       - FY27 organic growth \u2248 6.75\