mbursement add complexity, but the cash-flow mechanics are transparent.\n\nStep 2-2. Moat assessment (0\u20133 each):\n  Intangible assets (brand, patents, FDA approvals): 3\n  Switching costs (physician training, hospital supply chain): 3\n  Network effects: 1\n  Cost advantage (scale manufacturing, global distribution): 2\n  Economies of scale (R&D $2.9B, 180+ clinical trials): 3\n  Regulatory barriers: 3\n  Data moat (clinical registries, device telemetry): 2\n  TOTAL: 17/21 \u2192 Wide moat.\n  Moat direction: Wide, STABLE-to-WIDENING.\n  Widening evidence: US PFA share +8pts (CAS +78\u201380% FY26); CRM mid-single\n  digit growth; Hugo surgical system expanded indications (FDA filings);\n  Stealth AXiS cleared for spine/cranial/ENT [Actual, press release FY26 Q4].\n  Narrowing signals: diabetes competition (Insulet, Dexcom), Boston Scientific\n  in PFA, Intuitive in robotics.\n\nStep 2-3. Lynch classification: STALWART.\n  Checkpoints: Revenue growth 4\u20138%, FCF margin ~15%, dividend 3.1%, long\n  runway. Valuation should be 10\u201320x forward earnings \u2014 at 15.7x FY27\n  non-GAAP EPS, MDT is within the buy range [Estimate].\n\nStep 2-4. Financial strength scorecard:\n  \u2022 Revenue CAGR 3-yr (FY23\u2013FY26): (36.364/31.227)^(1/3)-1 = 5.2% [Arithmetic]\n  \u2022 Last 4 quarters YoY revenue: +8.4% reported / +5.8% organic [Actual]\n  \u2022 Operating margin (3-yr avg): 17.2% GAAP [Arithmetic]\n  \u2022 GAAP EPS FY26: $3.73, +3.3% y/y [Actual, press release]\n  \u2022 Non-GAAP EPS FY26: $5.53, +0.7% y/y [Actual]\n  \u2022 ROE: 9.8% [Aggregator-vendor computation]; GAAP ROIC: 7.6% [Estimate]\n  \u2022 Non-GAAP ROIC: ~10.5% [Estimate]\n  \u2022 FCF margin FY26: 14.9% [Actual]; FCF conversion vs non-GAAP NI: 76%\n    [Actual, company]\n  \u2022 Net debt: $19.99B [Estimate: component sum minus cash+ST inv]\n  \u2022 Net debt / EBITDA: 2.1x [Estimate]\n  \u2022 Interest coverage (EBIT / interest expense): ~9.0x [Estimate, using FY24\n    interest expense $0.719B as proxy; FY25\u201326 interest expense not in pack]\n  Judgment: GOOD (balanced, investment-grade A/A3, but not stellar on\n  unadjusted returns).\n\nStep 2-5. Capital allocation scorecard (0\u20133 each, total 15):\n  1. Buyback efficiency: 1 \u2014 1-yr net share issuance -0.1% [Arithmetic];\n     dilution offset, but no aggressive buyback below intrinsic value.\n  2. M&A track record: 2 \u2014 small tuck-ins (CathWorks, Scientia Vascular,\n     SPR Therapeutics) are within competence; legacy Covidien integration\n     produced impairments (no [Actual] impairment data in pack, so -0).\n  3. Capex efficiency: 2 \u2014 Incremental ROIC estimated 9\u201312% [Assumption],\n     above WACC but below 20% threshold.\n  4. Rationality of mix: 2 \u2014 R&D 2.9B + dividend 3.6B + buybacks 0.6B\n     (4.2B total returned) [Actual, company]; balanced but not optimal.\n  5. Guidance accuracy: 2 \u2014 FY26 Q4 revenue beat implied guidance by 90bps\n     [Actual]; FY27 EPS guide below consensus, mixed record.\n  TOTAL: 9/15.\n  Insider ownership bonus: CEO/mgmt 0.32% \u2014 no points; no cluster insider\n  buying disclosed [Unconfirmed]. Final: 9/15.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nStep 2.5-1. R&D capitalization:\n  FY26 R&D = $2.873B [Actual, macrotrends/10-K press release].\n  Capitalize and amortize over 5 years (straight-line):\n  Amortization \u2248 $2.70B [Estimate on steady-state R&D ~$2.7\u20132.9B].\n  Adjusted Operating Income = GAAP OI $6.467B + R&D $2.873B \u2212 Amort. $2.70B\n  \u2248 $6.64B [Estimate].\n  Adjusted Invested Capital = GAAP IC $69.45B [Estimate] + unamortized R&D\n  \u2248 $11.9B [Estimate] = $81.35B.\n  Adjusted ROIC (GAAP basis) = $6.64B \u00d7 (1\u22120.18) / $81.35B = 6.7% [Estimate].\n  Non-GAAP adjusted ROIC = ($8.856B + $0.17B) \u00d7 0.82 / $81.35B = 9.1%\n  [Estimate].\n\nStep 2.5-2. SBC treatment:\n  FY26 SBC = $0.457B [Actual per section 5; vendor scalar #2 matches at\n  $0.457B \u2014 period confirmed as fiscal year].\n  Adjusted FCF = Reported FCF $5.426B \u2212 SBC $0.457B = $4.969B [Estimate].\n  Adjusted FCF/share = $4.969B / 1.280B = $3.88 [Estimate].\n\nStep 2.5-3. Operating lease capitalization:\n  Operating leases FY26 = $1.188B [Actual]; finance leases $0.060B [Actual].\n  Adjusted net debt = LT noncurrent $26.173B + current portion $1.788B +\n  finance leases $0.060B + operating leases $1.188B \u2212 cash $1.949B \u2212 ST\n  investments $7.271B = $19.99B [Estimate].\n  NOTE: Short-term borrowings for FY26 are [Unconfirmed]; if a material\n  revolver balance exists, net debt is understated by that amount.\n\nStep 2.5-4. Brand/data assets:\n  No reliable brand-value figure retrieved [Unconfirmed]; medtech brand\n  value not material to DCF. Data moat embedded in switching costs \u2014 not\n  separately capitalized.\n\nStep 2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC gap:\n  GAAP ROIC 7.6% [Estimate] vs adjusted 6.7% [Estimate] \u2014 the adjustment\n  LOWERS ROIC because the R&D asset addition raises invested capital; the\n  gap (\u22120.9pp) is not material. Non-GAAP ROIC ~10.5% unadjusted vs 9.1%\n  adjusted \u2014 still above WACC 7.4%. No >5pp flag.\n\nStep 2.5-6. Owner Earnings:\n  Owner Earnings (FY26) = NI $4.801B +