sion for general surgery/GYN [Actual]; approvals\n     could re-rate robotics optionality.\n  4. MiniMed remaining 90% stake: IPO at $5.6B [Actual]; any future\n     monetization/distribution could surface value.\n  5. Non-GAAP margin recovery: FY26 tariff drag 50bps + Blackstone 45bps\n     [Actual]; if tariff relief occurs, margin recovers to prior trajectory.\n\n  RISKS:\n  1. PFA competition: Boston Scientific Farapulse (dominant share) and\n     Abbott Volt could stall MDT\u2019s +8pt share gain.\n  2. Guidance credibility: FY27 EPS guide $5.95 vs consensus $6.06 [Actual] \u2014\n     a negative signal on margin confidence.\n  3. Tariffs/China VBP: 50bps margin drag in FY26 [Actual]; if tariffs\n     escalate, 2027 non-GAAP margin <23.5% breaks the thesis.\n  4. Elliott Management activism: governance reform demand may turn into a\n     proxy fight [Actual per research brief \u2014 verify].\n  5. FCF conversion: 76% of non-GAAP NI [Actual] \u2014 if DSO/inventory\n     deterioration persists, owner earnings disappoint.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n  Common bear triggers shared across a typical multi-asset book:\n    \u2022 Rates up: correlates with long-duration quality; MDT beta to 10Y\n      ~ \u22120.3 [Assumption] \u2014 currently a headwind.\n    \u2022 Dollar up: MDT ~22% ex-US sales (assumption) \u2192 negative.\n    \u2022 Healthcare regulation/tariffs: shared with ABBV, BSX, JNJ \u2014 avoid\n      tripling up.\n    \u2022 Recession: elective procedures fall; MDT historically \u22125\u201310% vs SPX\n      \u221220\u201330% [Estimate].\n  Stress correlation: MDT vs SPX tail correlation ~0.85 [Assumption, 2020/2022\n  pattern]; CVaR (95%, 1-month) \u2248 \u22128% to \u221212% for MDT standalone [Estimate];\n  in a 10% position, portfolio CVaR impact \u2248 \u22121.0pp.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 8. MONITORING RULES (THESIS KPIs & PRE-MORTEM)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n  KPI thresholds that trigger re-evaluation:\n  \u2022 Organic revenue growth: <4.5% in FY27 Q1\u2013Q2 \u2192 downgrade thesis.\n  \u2022 Non-GAAP operating margin: <23.0% in any quarter \u2192 downgrade.\n  \u2022 Cardiac Ablation Solutions growth: <30% in any quarter \u2192 thesis broken.\n  \u2022 FCF conversion (vs non-GAAP NI): <70% for 2 consecutive quarters \u2192 reduce.\n  \u2022 Net debt/EBITDA: >3.0x \u2192 review balance-sheet strategy.\n  \u2022 Share count: >1.30B \u2192 SBC offsetting buybacks, downgrade.\n  \u2022 Hugo RAS: <50 systems placed/year \u2192 robotics optionality unproven.\n\n  PRE-MORTEM (5-year failure \u2014 \"Why is MDT at $60 in 2031?\"):\n  1. PFA war lost: Farapulse/Volt dominate, MDT CAS growth <15%, CV growth\n     <2%. Early warning: CAS <30%, CV <5%.\n  2. Robotics capital destruction: Hugo fails against Intuitive/J&J; $5B+\n     cumulative R&D/capex written off. Early warning: placement/utilization\n     misses.\n  3. Margin quagmire: tariffs >100bps, China VBP, Elliott proxy fight \u2192\n     non-GAAP margin 22%. Early warning: margin <23%, China revenue \u221210%.\n  4. Macro/rates: 10Y >5.5%, WACC 8.0%+, DCF breaks below $78. Early warning:\n     10Y >5.25%, credit spread widening.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 9. RED TEAM\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n  Step 9-1. Short thesis (5\u20137 bullets):\n  1. FY27 EPS guidance ($5.90\u20136.00) is BELOW consensus ($6.06) [Actual] \u2014\n     management is signaling that revenue momentum is not converting to\n     profit.\n  2. FCF conversion of 76% of non-GAAP NI [Actual] means \"earnings quality\"\n     is underwhelming; adjusted FCF/share $3.88 vs non-GAAP EPS $5.53 = a\n     30% cash gap [Estimate].\n  3. Net debt ~$20B [Estimate] with 10Y at 4.70% (and rising); refinancing\n     of $1.788B current portion [Actual] at higher coupons will drain FCF.\n  4. PFA growth (+80%) is from a small base; Boston Scientific is the\n     category leader and Abbott is entering \u2014 MDT\u2019s +8pts of US share is\n     against a far larger incumbent.\n  5. Hugo is 15+ years late to robotics; Intuitive has an installed base of\n     ~8,000+ systems; J&J brings scale \u2014 a 3-player space with pricing\n     pressure.\n  6. MiniMed IPO priced at ~$5.6B for a $3.1B revenue business (1.8x sales)\n     [Actual/Estimate] \u2014 a low multiple that reveals the market\u2019s skepticism\n     about the diabetes turnaround.\n  7. Elliott Management pressure [Actual per research brief] may force a\n     break-up where the sum-of-the-parts trades BELOW the whole.\n  8. Dividend growing slower than EPS implies the payout ratio is\n     constrained; the 49-yr streak is a marketing asset, not a valuation\n     floor.\n\n  Step 9-2. Logic combat:\n    Long logic strength: 6/10 (wide moat, FCF yield ~4.5%, PFA/Hugo options,\n    valuation 12% below base IV).\n    Short logic strength: 5/10 (guidance miss, FCF gap, competition, activist\n    overhang).\n    Gap = 1.0 < 2.0 \u2192 no conviction downgrade.\n\n  Step 9-3. Adversarial data:\n    No Hindenburg-style report exists for MDT [Unconfirmed \u2014 not retrieved].\n    Main adversarial pressure comes from Elliott\u2019s governance campaign\n    [Actual per research brief; verify via SEC filings]. TipRanks risk\n    section cites \"legal & regulatory = top risk category, 34 risks\"\n    [Estimate \u2014 third-party aggregation].\n\n  Step 9-4. Killed arguments (and the conditions that revive them):\n    \u2022 \"MDT is a value trap \u2014 growth has not shown.\" KILLED by FY26 actual\n      organic +5.8% and FY27 guide +6.75\u20137.25% [Actual]. REVIVES if FY27 Q1\n      organic <4.5%.\n    \u2022 \"The spin-off destroys value.\" KILLED because MDT retains 90.03%\n      control [Actual]; the IPO creates a public currency without loss of\n      consolidation. REVIVES if MDT distributes the remaining stake at a\n      discount (mini-mini IPO below $5.6B).\n    \u2022 \"Rates kill the dividend.\" KILLED because dividend $2.88 is 51% of\n      FY27 guide mid-point $5.95; FCF yield 4.2% vs 10Y 4.7% \u2014 close but not\n      stranded. REVIVES if 10Y >5.5%.\n    \u2022 \"Margins are dead.\" KILLED by decomposing FY26 drag: 50bps tariffs +\n      45bps one-time Blackstone [Actual]; excluding those, non-GAAP margin\n      would have expanded. REVIVES if tariffs persist >100bps and non-GAAP\n      margin <23%.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS (7 CATEGORIES, 37-POINT CHECK)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n  A. Methodology: PASS \u2014 DCF is primary, multiples triangulate, no DCF-only.\n  B. Valuation: PASS \u2014 WACC, terminal growth, margin, revenue all\n     sensitivity-tested; V-shape tornado identified top-3 KPIs.\n  C. Bias: PASS \u2014 The author has no MDT position; check against\n     overconfidence: base-case probability held at 50%, not 60%+; MoS 11.9%\n     is labeled \"Limited,\" not \"Strong.\"\n  D. Consistency: PASS \u2014 FY26 revenue $36.364B matches SEC 10-K and press\n     release; FY26 EPS $3.73 GAAP matches; no mixing of time-points (T0 =\n     2026-