u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 2-1. Business Understanding (3 sentences)\nMedtronic designs, manufactures, and sells medical devices across\ncardiac rhythm and heart failure, neuromodulation, spine and cranial\ntech, surgical instruments, monitoring, and diabetes (MiniMed \u2014\nbeing spun off). Its model is hospital-centric: high-switching-cost\nimplantable hardware + consumables + software support contracts,\nsold through long-tenured clinical relationships. Profitability\ncomes from a diversified, annuity-like installed base with 55-65%\ngross margins.\nUnderstandability: MEDIUM-HIGH. (Medical device workflow is complex;\ncash-flow mechanics are simple.)\n\nStep 2-2. Moat Assessment (+ Moat Dynamics)\n\u2022 Intangible assets (brand, patents): 2/3 \u2014 (strong but not\n  consumer-franchise strength)\n\u2022 Switching costs: 3/3 \u2014 implantable devices, surgeon training,\n  hospital inventory\n\u2022 Network effects: 1/3 \u2014 limited but exists in monitoring data/\n  installed-base ecosystem\n\u2022 Cost advantage: 2/3 \u2014 scale manufacturing, global supply chain\n\u2022 Economies of scale: 3/3 \u2014 $36B revenue, 10%+ share in multiple\n  categories\n\u2022 Regulatory barriers: 3/3 \u2014 FDA/CE/PMDA; high approval bar\n\u2022 Data moat: 2/3 \u2014 device telemetry, CareLink, surgical data\nTOTAL: 16/21 \u2192 WIDE MOAT. Direction: WIDENING in CV (PFA share gains)\nand Surgical (Hugo); STABLE in Neuro; NARROWING in Diabetes\n(competitive loss to Dexcom/Tandem \u2014 but being divested).\n\nStep 2-3. Lynch Classification: STALWART with Fast-Growing divisions.\nVerdict: Fits large-cap stalwart; CV portfolio is the accelerator.\nCheckpoint: sustained share gains, no margin collapse \u2014 currently\npassing.\n\nStep 2-4. Financial Strength Scorecard (all T-1 = FY ended 2026-04-24)\n\u2022 Revenue growth: 5.8% organic FY26; 3-yr revenue CAGR ~4.7%\n  [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 Adj. operating margin: 24.4% non-GAAP, FY26 [Actual]; GAAP 17.8%\n\u2022 FY26 non-GAAP diluted EPS: $5.53 (+0.7% y/y; -2.0% cc)\n  [Actual, co. release]\n\u2022 ROE: 9.84% GAAP [Aggregator]; ROIC \u2248 13.5-14% [Estimate]\n\u2022 FCF margin: $5.426B / $36.364B \u2248 14.9% [Arithmetic]; FCF\n  conversion 76% of non-GAAP net income [Actual, co. release]\n\u2022 Net debt / EBITDA: 1.9x (vendor, LTM) [Aggregator]; my recalc:\n  net debt incl. ST investments $18.7B / EBITDA ~$9.5B \u2248 2.0x\n  [Estimate]\n\u2022 Interest coverage: GAAP EBIT $6.467B / est. interest ~$0.55B \u2248\n  11.8x [Estimate]\nJUDGMENT: GOOD-EXCELLENT (improving growth, stable margins, ample\nliquidity, slight leverage).\n\nStep 2-5. Capital Allocation Scorecard (/15)\n1. Buyback efficiency: 1/3 \u2014 buyback only offsets SBC; 1-yr net\n   issuance -0.1%, 3-yr +1.4% [Arithmetic]\n2. M&A track record: 2/3 \u2014 heavy prior-year impairments (Covidien\n   goodwill); recent tuck-ins (CathWorks, Scientia Vascular) smaller\n   and targeted\n3. Capex efficiency: 2/3 \u2014 capex ~5.2% of revenue; incremental ROIC\n   unproven but guided improvement\n4. Rationality of mix: 2/3 \u2014 spin-off simplifies portfolio; dividend\n   hike continues\n5. Guidance accuracy: 3/3 \u2014 Q4 FY26 beat implied guidance by 90bps\n   [Actual]; FY26 EPS raised mid-year [Actual, co. release]\nTOTAL: 10/15.\nInsider adjustments: CEO/insider ownership 0.32% \u2014 negligible (0);\nno notable 6-mo insider cluster buy/sell in pack [Unconfirmed].\nScore: 10/15.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 2.5-1. R&D Capitalization\n\u2022 FY26 R&D: $2.873B [Actual \u2014 macrotrends/company press release].\n\u2022 Capitalize; amortize over 4 years (straight-line). Adjusted OI =\n  $6.467B + $2.873B - amortization (~$2.15B/year on 4-yr rolling\n  average) \u2248 +$0.72B \u2192 adjusted GAAP EBIT \u2248 $7.19B [Estimate].\n\u2022 Adjusted invested capital = $91.0B - current liabilities $11.7B +\n  unamortized R&D (~$7.0B) \u2248 $86.3B [Estimate].\n\nStep 2.5-2. SBC / Share-based pay\n\u2022 FY26 SBC $0.457B [Filed]. Treated as cash expense \u2014 reduces FCF:\n  Adjusted FCF = $5.426B - SBC $0.457B \u2248 $4.97B. Reported FCF is\n  accordingly overstated by ~8.4% [Arithmetic].\n\nStep 2.5-3. Operating leases\n\u2022 FY26 operating leases $1.188B [Filed]. De minimis vs $138B\n  capital structure; included in debt for completeness.\n\nStep 2.5-4. Brand/Data assets\n\u2022 Not quantified. Medical-device brand equity is real but modest vs\n  consumer; no adjustment [Unconfirmed].\n\nStep 2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC\n\u2022 Adjusted NOPAT \u2248 $7.19B \u00d7 (1 - 20% tax est.) \u2248 $5.75B.\n\u2022 Adjusted IC \u2248 $86.3B \u2192 Adjusted ROIC \u2248 6.7% (if using total\n  assets-derived IC); if excluding goodwill/intangibles from IC\n  (~$45.7B goodwill + ~$14.4B intangibles est.), ROIC \u2248 19-21%\n  [Estimate]. GAAP ROIC \u2248 9.8-10%. Gap due entirely to acquisition-\n  related goodwill and R&D capitalization. Explains management\n  incentive to show \"ROIC > WACC\" on cash basis. Verdict: economic\n  ROIC (ex-goodwill) > WACC; accounting ROIC marginal.\n\nStep 2.5-6. Owner Earnings (Buffett)\nOE = NI $4.801B + D&A $2.958B - maintenance capex (est. 3.5% of\nrevenue \u2248 $1.27B) - \u0394WC (~+$2.19B use in FY26) \u2248 $4.3B [Estimate \u2014\nvolatile due to WC swing]. Normalized OE (ex-WC) \u2248 $6.5B. Note this\nis GAAP-based; non-GAAP normalized \u2248 $7.5B.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 3. VALUATION \u2014 ENGINE 1 (DCF + MULTIPLES)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 3-1. DCF\n\n**Discount-Rate Derivation (WACC)**\n\u2022 Risk-free rate (10Y UST): 4.7% [Actual]\n\u2022 ERP: 4.5% [Assumption]\n\u2022 Beta: vendor states 0.566 [Aggregator]; I reject the vendor beta\n  for WACC because it is demonstrably too low for a company with\n  2x net-debt/EBITDA and med-tech cyclicality; use 0.80 (5-yr\n  adjusted beta for MDT \u2248 0.7-0.9 [Assumption]).\n\u2022 Cost of Equity = 4.7% + 0.80 \u00d7 4.5% = 8.3%\n\u2022 Pre-tax cost of debt: 5.0% [Estimate \u2014 A1/A+ med-tech curve]\n\u2022 After-tax cost of debt = 5.0% \u00d7 (1 - 0.20) = 4.0%\n\u2022 Equity weight: 86% ($119.5B mkt cap); Debt weight: 14% (~$18.7B\n  net debt incl. leases & current portion, less cash + ST inv)\n\u2022 WACC = 0.86 \u00d7 8.3% + 0.14 \u00d7 4.0% = 7.7%. Use 7.5% (add 20bp for\n  event risk) [Assumption]. Check: at beta 0.566 WACC \u2248 6.9-7.0%;\n  at 0.65 WACC \u2248 7.2%. My WACC is deliberately conservative.\n\n**Effective Tax Rate**: ~20% [Assumption \u2014 the pack withheld the\nconsolidated rate; non-GAAP and GAAP FX-neutral effective rates at\nMDT have run 14-21% over FY19-26; I use 20% for conservatism].\n\n**Forecast: Continuing Operations (ex-MiniMed retained value added\nseparately)**\n\nBasis: FY26 reported revenue $36.364B [Actual]; whole-company adj.\noperating profit $8.856B (24.4% margin) [Actual] \u2014 includes ~$300M\nMiniMed NOI [Estimate]. Continuing adj. EBIT \u2248 $8.55B. GAAP EBIT\ncontinuing \u2248 $6.47B - ~$0.25B MiniMed \u2248 $6.2B [Estimate].\n\n| FY | Rev $B [Assumption] | OpM% GAAP [Assumption] | EBIT $B | D&A $B [Assumption] | SBC $B | Capex $B | \u0394WC $B [Assumption] | Tax 20% $B | FCF $B |\n|----|----|----|----|----|----|----|----|----|----|\n| FY27 | 35.50 (incl. 53rd wk) | 18.0% | 6.39 | 3.05 | 0.46 | 1.90 | -0.50 (source of cash) | 1.28 | 7.22 |\n| FY28 | 37.63 (6.0% org) | 18.3% | 6.89 | 3.15 | 0.48 | 2.00 | -0.30 | 1.38 | 7.28 |\n| FY29 | 39.51 (5.0% org) | 18.6% | 7.35 | 3.25 | 0.50 | 2.10 | -0.20 | 1.47 | 7.43 |\n| FY30 | 41.09 (4.0% org) | 18.8% | 7.72 | 3.35 | 0.52 | 2.20 | -0.10 | 1.54 | 7.50 |\n| FY31 | 42.32 (3.0% org) | 19.0% | 8.04 | 3.45 | 0.54 | 2.30 | 0.00 | 1.61 | 7.56 |\n\nForecast drivers sourced:\n\u2022 FY27 revenue = whole-co. 6.75\u20137.25% organic guidance [Actual] \u00d7\n  $36.3B adjusted revenue \u2192 $38.8-38.9B; minus diabetes (~$3.2B) \u2192\n  continuing ~$35.6-35.7B. I use 35.50 [Estimate].\n\u2022 FY28-31 growth: 6.0%\u21923.0% decel [Assumption]. This is the\n  critical judgment \u2014 beyond guided year there is no company\n  guidance. Sensitivity shown below.\n\u2022 FY27 margins: guided \"modest adjusted EPS expansion\" [Actual];\n  GAAP margin at 18.0% implies flat-to-slightly-up [Assumption].\n\u2022 D&A \u2248 8.2-8.3% of revenue (consistent with FY26 2.958/36.364 =\n  8.1%) [Arithmetic]. SBC \u2248 1.2% of revenue [Arithmetic].\n\u2022 Capex \u2248 5.2-5.4% of revenue (FY26 actual 1.904/36.364 = 5.2%)\n  [Arithmetic].\n\u2022 Tax 20% [Assumption].\n\n**Terminal value**: g = 2.5% (\u2248 long-run nominal GDP floor)\n[Assumption]. Terminal FCF = $7.56B \u00d7 1.025 = $7.75B. TV =\n$7.75B / (0.075 - 0.025) = $155.0B \u2192 present value at 7.5% (5 yrs)\n= $108.0B.\n\n**DCF math** (discount factor 7.5%):\nFY27: 7.22 / 1.075 = 6.72\nFY28: 7.28 / 1.156 = 6.30\nFY29: 7.43 / 1.242 = 5.98\nFY30: 7.50 / 1.335 = 5.62\nFY31: 7.56 / 1.436 = 5.26\nPV of explicit FCF = $29.9B\nPV of terminal value = $108.0B\nEV = $137.9B [Arithmetic]\n\n**Net debt adjustment** (my chosen components, stated):\n\u2022 LT debt noncurrent: $26.173B [Filed]\n\u2022 + Current portion: $1.788B [Filed]\n\u2022 + Finance leases: $0.060B [Filed]\n\u2022 + Operating leases: $1.188B [Filed]\n\u2022 - Cash: $1.949B [Filed]\n\u2022 - Short-term investments: $7.271B [Filed]\n\u2022 Net debt = $26.173 + 1.788 + 0.060 + 1.188 - 1.949 - 7.271 =\n  $19.989B [Arithmetic]\n\n**MiniMed stake**: I value the retained interest at $4.50/share\n[Estimate \u2014 range $2.50-6.00]. Basis: IPO of 10% raised $560M\n[Actual, press reports] implies ~$5.6B valuation; deal coverage\nreferences $7.9B [Estimate, press]; using $6B mid and 90%\nretained after IPO \u2192 MDT stake \u2248 $5.4B \u2248 $4.20/share. Add eventual\nfull split-off value not yet recognized; I use $4.50 [Assumption].\n\nEquity value = EV $137.9B - Net debt $20.0B + MiniMed stake $5.8B\n= $123.7B.\nPer share on 1,288.1M shares [Filed] = $96.0/share.\n\nRANGE DISCLOSURE: On WACC 7.0% \u2192 $106; WACC 8.0% \u2192 $88.\nOn FY28-31 growth (5.5/4.5/3.5/2.5) \u2192 $94.4; on\n(6.5/5.5/4.5/3.5) \u2192 $97.8.\nFair-value range: $88-$106. Central: $96.\n\n**Step 3-2. Multiples cross-check**\n\u2022 P/E: FY27 guided EPS $5.90-6.00 [Actual] \u2192 15.6-15.8x forward.\n  Peer median (large-cap med-device) \u2248 17-19x forward (BSX, SYK,\n  ABT) [Estimate \u2014 external]. Justified forward multiple for MDT at\n  5-6% organic growth and 24% margins: 16-17x. \u2192 $95-102.\n\u2022 EV/EBITDA: EV $138B / adj. EBITDA (~$9.5B incl. MiniMed) \u2248 14.5x.\n  Sector \u2248 14-17x. Midpoint supports \u2248 $95-100.\n\u2022 P/FCF: $138B / $8.0B \u2248 17x \u2014 consistent with historical.\n\u2022 PEG: 1.8 trailing (pack); on forward growth ~2.0 \u2014 fair, not cheap.\nMultiple cross-check conclusion: $95-102.\n\n**Reconciled intrinsic value: $95.50 (central) with 80% CI\n$82-$110.** [Assumption-set; single point discouraged]\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n3.5-1 Competitive response\n\u2022 If PFA penetration continues at 80% growth, BSX (Farapulse), ABT\n  (TactiFlex), and J&J will respond with price/tech escalation.\n  Impact on MDT: -1 (modest margin pressure in portion of CV).\n\u2022 Robotics: Intuitive remains dominant; Hugos wins only if\n  install-base traction continues. Impact: neutral.\n3.5-2 Reflexivity\n\u2022 Positive: strong price \u2192 SBC attract talent, paper for M&A.\n\u2022 Negative: low price \u2192 Elliott pressure already materialized\n  (constructive settlement, board seats Aug 2025) [Actual \u2014 press\n  release]; further weakness could force disposals or strategy\n  shifts.\n3.5-3 Customer behavior\n\u2022 Procedure mix shifting to outpatient/ambulatory; affects capital\n  equipment attach economics modestly. LTV/CAC stable [Assumption].\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nPrior: base-rate informed (Sec 1.5). Updates from FY26 Q4 beat\n(+90bps vs implied guidance) and FY27 guide 6.75-7.25% [Actual]\nraise posterior.\n\n| Scenario | Probability | Price in 12M | Notes |\n|----|----|----|----|\n| Bear | 25% | $78-85 | Tariffs persist; mini-spin delays; PFA competition; margins flat; P/E compresses to 14x |\n| Base | 50% | $95-103 | 6% organic growth, margins stable, spin closes, 16.5x multiple |\n| Bull | 25% | $108-118 | 7%+ organic, Hugo/Affera accelerations, MiniMed listed at $8B+, margins +100bps |\n\nExpected 12M price = 0.25\u00d782 + 0.50\u00d799 + 0.25\u00d7113 = $98.25.\nExpected return \u2248 5.2% + dividend 3.1% \u2248 8.3%/yr \u2014 adequate, not\nexceptional.\n50% CI: $92-$106; 80% CI: $82-$115. Margin of safety = ($95.5 -\n$93.35)/$95.5 = 2.3% \u2192 NONE-TO-LIMITED.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 4.5. TIME-HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u2022 Market-implied horizon: price = 15.7x next-year EPS; at 6%\n  sustainable growth, the market is paying for ~8-9 years of\n  earnings power [Estimate].\n\u2022 My horizon: 3-5 years.\n\u2022 Spread: market already capitalizes visible growth; no multi-year\n  horizon gap. Arbitrage opportunity: NONE.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2