s and sells\n      implantable and interventional medical devices across cardiovascular\n      (CRM, defibrillation, PFA, renal denervation), neuroscience (spine,\n      neuromodulation), medical-surgical (surgical robotics, endoscopy,\n      acute-care monitoring) and diabetes (insulin pumps/CGM). It operates in\n      ~150 countries with \u224850%+ non-US revenue [Estimate]. Its economic engine\n      is installed-base recurring procedure volume, surgeon/hospital switching\n      costs, and pipeline-driven share gains.\n      Understandability: HIGH.\n2.2   Moat score (0\u20133 each):\n        Intangible assets (brand/patents): 2\n        Switching costs (physician/hospital): 3\n        Network effects: 1\n        Cost advantage: 1\n        Economies of scale: 3\n        Regulatory barriers: 3\n        Data moat: 2\n        TOTAL: 15/21 \u2192 WIDE moat.\n      Moat dynamics: STABLE overall; WIDENING in cardiac ablation (Affera PFA\n      gaining 8pts US share in Q4 FY26 [Actual - company release]); NARROWING\n      in diabetes (Insulet, Tandem, Abbott Lingo competition; MiniMed business\n      being separated) [Estimate - research brief].\n2.3   Lynch classification: STALWART (large, steady, dividend-grower with fast-\n      growing product pockets). Core checkpoint: EPS growth \u2248 revenue growth +\n      buyback + modest margin expansion; FY26 adjusted EPS +0.7% [Actual] vs\n      revenue +8.4% reported [Actual] \u2192 margin dilutive year; FY27 guided\n      adjusted EPS $5.90\u20136.00 (+7.2% at mid) [Actual - company guidance].\n2.4   Financial strength scorecard:\n      - Revenue 5-yr CAGR (FY21\u2013FY26): 36.364/30.117^(1/5)\u22121 = +3.8%\n        [Arithmetic].\n      - FY26 GAAP OI margin: 17.8% [Arithmetic]; 12-yr median: 17.9%\n        [Arithmetic]. Strength: stable, slightly below peak.\n      - FY26 FCF margin: 5.426/36.364 = 14.9% [Arithmetic]. FCF/OCF\n        conversion: 5.426/7.330 = 74.0% [Arithmetic]; SBC-adjusted FCF =\n        4.969B [Arithmetic].\n      - ROE: 9.8% [Aggregator vendor]; GAAP ROIC est. 6.8% [Estimate]\n        (depressed by \u2248$40B goodwill from Covidien [Estimate - not separately\n        in pack]).\n      - Net debt/EBITDA: $18.741B / $9.425B = 2.0x [Arithmetic on filed EBIT +\n        D&A]; net debt/adjusted EBIT (8.856B non-GAAP [Actual - co. release]):\n        2.1x [Estimate].\n      - Interest coverage: FY26 interest expense not held [Unconfirmed]; FY24\n        interest $0.719B [Filed]; est. coverage \u2248 8\u20139x [Estimate].\n      - Net cash vs net debt: net debt \u2248 $18.7B [Arithmetic]; no going-concern\n        stress.\n      VERDICT: GOOD.\n2.5   Capital allocation scorecard (0\u201315):\n        Buyback efficiency: 1/3 (3-yr share count CAGR +1.4%, i.e., net\n        issuance [Arithmetic]; SBC nearly offsets buybacks).\n        M&A track record: 2/3 (tuck-ins in PFA, neurovascular, neuromodulation;\n        no large impairments; but 5-yr ROIC > WACC on M&A not established\n        [Estimate]).\n        Capex efficiency: 2/3 (capex 5.2% of revenue [Arithmetic]; incremental\n        ROIC est. ~12\u201315%, above WACC but <20% [Estimate]).\n        Rationality of mix: 2/3 (dividend + R&D + tuck-ins, sensible).\n        Guidance accuracy: 3/3 (FY26 raised guidance; Q4 beat by 90bps\n        [Actual - company release]).\n        Insider: no bonus/penalty (CEO ownership <5%, no cluster buy/sell\n        observed [Unconfirmed]).\n        TOTAL: 10/15.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2.5 \u2014 INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n2.5.1 R&D capitalization: FY26 R&D $2.873B [Estimate - Macrotrends; not in\n      pack], FY25 \u2248 $2.73B [Estimate], FY24 \u2248 $2.60B [Estimate].\n      Using 3-yr straight-line amortization:\n        Amortization = (2.873+2.732+2.602)/3 \u2248 $2.736B [Estimate].\n        Adjusted OI = 6.467 + 2.873 \u2212 2.736 = $6.604B [Arithmetic].\n        Unamortized R&D asset \u2248 2.873 + (2/3)(2.732) + (1/3)(2.602)\n                       \u2248 5.56B [Estimate].\n2.5.2 SBC treatment: Adjusted FCF = 5.426 \u2212 0.457 = $4.969B [Arithmetic].\n      Per-share owner FCF on 1.280B shares = $3.88 [Arithmetic].\n2.5.3 Operating leases: add $1.188B [Filed] to debt.\n      Adjusted net debt = 18.741 + 1.188 + 0.060 (finance leases [Filed]) =\n      $19.99B [Arithmetic].\n2.5.4 Brand/data: Brand value not reliably quantified [Unconfirmed].\n2.5.5 Adjusted ROIC:\n        Adjusted NOPAT = 6.604 \u2212 0.457 SBC = 6.147 \u00d7 (1 \u2212 0.16 tax\n        [Estimate]) \u2248 $5.16B [Estimate].\n        Adjusted IC = 68.204 (equity 49.463 + total debt 27.961 \u2212 cash/ST\n        investments 9.220) + 5.56 (R&D) + 1.25 (leases) \u2248 $74.0B [Estimate].\n        Adj. ROIC \u2248 5.16/74.0 = 7.0% [Estimate].\n      GAAP ROIC \u2248 6.8% [Estimate]. Gap vs adjusted: \u22480.2pp, not material.\n      NOTE: ROIC is low, but reported equity includes ~$40B goodwill; on\n      tangible invested capital (excluding goodwill/intangibles [Unconfirmed \u2014\n      segments not held]), ROIC is likely in the 13\u201316% range [Estimate].\n2.5.6 Owner earnings (Buffett):\n        Owner Earnings = NI 4.801 + D&A 2.958 \u2212 maintenance capex ~1.50\n        [Assumption \u2014 80% of FY26 capex] \u2212 \u0394WC ~0.60 [Estimate based on\n        AR+Inv delta of 0.60 between FY25 and FY26 [Arithmetic]]\n        \u2248 $5.66B [Estimate].\n        Owner-earnings yield = 5.66 / 119.505 = 4.7% [Arithmetic].\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3 \u2014 VALUATION (ENGINE 1: DCF + MULTIPLES)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n3.1   Discount-rate derivation:\n      - Risk-free (10Y UST): 4.65% [Actual - FRED, 2026-08-21].\n      - Equity risk premium: 4.50% [Assumption].\n      - Beta: 0.75 [Assumption; vendor reports 0.566 [Aggregator] but window/\n        benchmark unknown; 0.75 better reflects medical-device cyclicality and\n        FDA/tariff exposure].\n      - Cost of equity = 4.65 + 0.75(4.50) = 8.03% [Arithmetic].\n      - Pre-tax cost of debt: 4.50% [Estimate \u2014 A-rated med-tech spread over\n        4.65% 10Y; pack interest expense implies ~3% coupon but refinancing\n        risk makes 4.5% the right marginal cost].\n      - Tax rate: 16% [Estimate \u2014 MDT non-GAAP nominal tax rate; GAAP ETR not\n        fully derivable from pack].\n      - After-tax cost of debt = 4.50%(1\u22120.16) = 3.78% [Arithmetic].\n      - Weights: E = 119.505 / (119.505+27.961) = 81.0%;\n        D = 27.961 / 147.466 = 19.0% [Arithmetic].\n      - WACC = 0.810(8.03%) + 0.190(3.78%) = 6.50 + 0.72 = 7.22% \u2248 7.2%\n        [Arithmetic].\n      - Base WACC used: 7.5% [Assumption \u2014 add ~30bps for FX volatility,\n        tariff/regulatory event risk not captured in beta; range 7.0\u20138.0%].\n3.2   Forecast path \u2014 explicit per year, FY27E\u2013FY36E ($B) [Assumptions in\n      brackets; each line tied to a source]:\n      Revenue growth:\n        FY27: +7.0% \u2192 $38.91B [Actual guidance 6.75\u20137.25% organic, incl. 53rd\n        week; no material FX assumption. Source: Medtronic June 3, 2026 release].\n        FY28: +5.5% \u2192 $41.05B [Assumption \u2014 above 5-yr CAGR 3.8% because PFA/\n        Hugo ramp; fading].\n        FY29: +5.0% \u2192 $43.10B [Assumption].\n        FY30: +4.5% \u2192 $45.04B [Assumption \u2014 industry CAGR ~5.4% per\n        MarketsandMarkets [Estimate]; large-cap discount).\n        FY31: +4.5% \u2192 $47.06B [Assumption].\n        FY32: +4.0% \u2192 $48.95B [Assumption].\n        FY33: +4.0% \u2192 $50.91B [Assumption].\n        FY34: +3.5% \u2192 $52.69B [Assumption].\n        FY35: +3.5% \u2192 $54.54B [Assumption].\n        FY36: +3.0% \u2192 $56.17B [Assumption \u2014 near long-run nominal GDP].\n        Long-term terminal growth: 3.0% [Assumption \u2014 = long-run nominal GDP].\n      GAAP operating margin (OI):\n        FY26 actual: 17.8% [Arithmetic on filed OI $6.467B / rev $36.364B].\n        FY27\u2013FY36: 17.9%, 18.2%, 18.5%, 18.7%, 18.9%, 19.1%, 19.2%, 19.3%,\n        19.4%, 19.5% [Assumption \u2014 gradual recovery toward FY18 peak 22.2%\n        [Arithmetic], capped at 19.5% to remain conservative; FY27 guided EPS\n        +7% on revenue +7% implies margin roughly flat [Estimate]].\n      Tax rate: 16% 