m (Elliott [Estimate \u2014 research brief]) reduces management\n         bandwidth and can force leverage-increasing M&A or poor exits.\n      7. GAAP ROIC \u2248 7% [Estimate] is BELOW WACC \u2014 the business earns less\n         than its cost of capital on an adjusted basis; \"quality-compounder\"\n         classification is generous.\n9.2   Logic combat:\n      Long thesis score: 7/10. Short thesis score: 6/10.\n      Gap = 1 (< 2) \u2192 Conviction downgrade applied (Section 5).\n      Core long advantage: filing-based cash generation ($5.426B FCF FY26\n      [Arithmetic]) is real; PFA/Hugo optionality is free at the current\n      no-growth price.\n      Core short advantage: margin trend is genuinely negative; revenue growth\n      contains artificial boosts (53rd week, easy comps, FX).\n9.3   Adversarial data: no current Hindenburg-type report exists [Unconfirmed];\n      risk-factor screen at TipRanks shows 34 regulatory risks [Estimate \u2014\n      research brief]. No accounting red flags in pack: Piotroski 7/7,\n      accruals \u22120.0274 [Arithmetic \u2014 filed-derived].\n9.4   Killed arguments:\n      - \"Hugo is a robotics game-changer\": killed at 50% weight because\n        Intuitive's installed base and procedural ecosystem dwarf MDT;\n        valid again only if Hugo placements exceed 100/quarter.\n      - \"PFA makes MDT a growth stock\": killed because cardiac ablation is\n        <10% of total revenue [Estimate]; valid again only if CV organic\n        sustains >9% for 8+ quarters.\n      - \"Spinoffs always create value\": killed because MiniMed's IPO priced\n        soft; valid again only if MMED trades >$25 [Unconfirmed price] and\n        MDT distributes the stake tax-free.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\