n  1. Revenue CAGR (trailing 5 FYs) = +3.8% [Arithmetic]; 12-year revenue history\n     shows low volatility (range ~+2%\u2013+8.4% organic) \u2014 a stable grower, not an\n     option story.\n  2. GAAP operating margin median = +17.9% over 12 years [Arithmetic]; band of\n     14.9%\u201322.2% \u2014 low dispersion, consistent with a defensive, diversified\n     incumbent.\n  3. FCF margin steady: FY26 FCF $5.426B / revenue $36.364B = 14.9% [Actual];\n     FCF ranged $3.6\u20136.0B across the 12-year window \u2014 reliable cash generation.\n  4. 49 consecutive annual dividend increases [Actual, company press release\n     2026-06-03]; dividend not a growth-optionality promise.\n\nTransition trigger to B (Quality Compounder):\n  \u2022 Non-GAAP ROIC ~10.5% [Estimate, see Layer 2.5] vs. WACC 7.4%\n    \u2192 Marginally above threshold; 3-year consistency holds (non-GAAP ROIC\n    9\u201311% estimated FY24\u2013FY26).\n  \u2022 50\u201380% of criteria met \u2192 per framework, use a BLENDED engine:\n    Engine 1 (80%) + Engine 3/quality-premium overlay (20%). This avoids\n    abandoning the stable-cash-flow anchor while acknowledging ROIC > WACC.\n\nStep 0-4. Why this engine:\n  \u2022 Engine 1 is appropriate because MDT\u2019s value derives from distributable\n    cash flow, not a single binary event or an unproven optionality.\n  \u2022 Errors avoided: Engine 4 (expectation-driven) would over-weight narrative\n    (PFA, Hugo) and under-weight the $5.4B FCF anchor; Engine 5 (binary) is\n    inapplicable \u2014 no single approval gate.\n  \u2022 If valued as a pure quality compounder at peer multiples (BSX ~25x\n    forward P/E), MDT would be overvalued; Engine 1\u2019s normalization is\n    conservative.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\